{
  "schemaVersion": 2,
  "bookCode": "RV10",
  "bookSlug": "rig-veda-book-10",
  "n": 72,
  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "n": 1,
      "refId": "RV10-72:1",
      "text": "translated by"
    },
    {
      "n": 2,
      "refId": "RV10-72:2",
      "text": "1. LET US with tuneful skill proclaim these generations of the Gods,",
      "original": "देवानां नु वयं जाना प्र वोचाम विपन्यया ।",
      "translit": "devānāṃ nu vayaṃ jānā pra vocāma vipanyayā |"
    },
    {
      "n": 3,
      "refId": "RV10-72:3",
      "text": "That one may see them when these hymns are chanted in a future age.",
      "original": "उक्थेषु शस्यमानेषु यः पश्यादुत्तरे युगे",
      "translit": "uktheṣu śasyamāneṣu yaḥ paśyāduttare yuge"
    },
    {
      "n": 4,
      "refId": "RV10-72:4",
      "text": "2. These Brahmanaspati produced with blast and smelting, like a Smith,",
      "original": "ब्रह्मणस्पतिरेता सं कर्मार इवाधमत् ।",
      "translit": "brahmaṇaspatiretā saṃ karmāra ivādhamat |"
    },
    {
      "n": 5,
      "refId": "RV10-72:5",
      "text": "Existence, in an earlier age of Gods, from Non-existence sprang.",
      "original": "देवानां पूर्व्ये युगेऽसतः सदजायत",
      "translit": "devānāṃ pūrvye yuge'sataḥ sadajāyata"
    },
    {
      "n": 6,
      "refId": "RV10-72:6",
      "text": "3. Existence, in the earliest age of Gods, from Non-existence sprang.",
      "original": "देवानां युगे प्रथमेऽसतः सदजायत ।",
      "translit": "devānāṃ yuge prathame'sataḥ sadajāyata |"
    },
    {
      "n": 7,
      "refId": "RV10-72:7",
      "text": "Thereafter were the regions born. This sprang from the Productive Power.",
      "original": "तदाशा अन्वजायन्त तदुत्तानपदस्परि",
      "translit": "tadāśā anvajāyanta taduttānapadaspari"
    },
    {
      "n": 8,
      "refId": "RV10-72:8",
      "text": "4. Earth sprang from the Productive Power the regions from the earth were born.",
      "original": "भूर्जज्ञ उत्तानपदो भुव आशा अजायन्त ।",
      "translit": "bhūrjajña uttānapado bhuva āśā ajāyanta |"
    },
    {
      "n": 9,
      "refId": "RV10-72:9",
      "text": "Daksa was born of Aditi, and Aditi was Daksa's Child.",
      "original": "अदितेर्दक्षो अजायत दक्षाद्वदितिः परि",
      "translit": "aditerdakṣo ajāyata dakṣādvaditiḥ pari"
    },
    {
      "n": 10,
      "refId": "RV10-72:10",
      "text": "5. For Aditi, O Daksa, she who is thy Daughter, was brought forth.",
      "original": "अदितिर्ह्यजनिष्ट दक्ष या दुहिता तव ।",
      "translit": "aditirhyajaniṣṭa dakṣa yā duhitā tava |"
    },
    {
      "n": 11,
      "refId": "RV10-72:11",
      "text": "After her were the blessed Gods born sharers of immortal life.",
      "original": "तां देवा अन्वजायन्त भद्रा अमृतबन्धवः",
      "translit": "tāṃ devā anvajāyanta bhadrā amṛtabandhavaḥ"
    },
    {
      "n": 12,
      "refId": "RV10-72:12",
      "text": "6. When ye, O Gods, in yonder deep close clasping one another stood,",
      "original": "यद्देवा अदः सलिले सुसंरब्धा अतिष्ठत ।",
      "translit": "yaddevā adaḥ salile susaṃrabdhā atiṣṭhata |"
    },
    {
      "n": 13,
      "refId": "RV10-72:13",
      "text": "Thence, as of dancers, from your feet a thickening cloud of dust arose.",
      "original": "अत्रा वो नृत्यतामिव तीव्रो रेणुरपायत",
      "translit": "atrā vo nṛtyatāmiva tīvro reṇurapāyata"
    },
    {
      "n": 14,
      "refId": "RV10-72:14",
      "text": "7. When, O ye Gods, like Yatis, ye caused all existing things to grow,",
      "original": "यद्देवा यतयो यथा भुवनान्यपिन्वत ।",
      "translit": "yaddevā yatayo yathā bhuvanānyapinvata |"
    },
    {
      "n": 15,
      "refId": "RV10-72:15",
      "text": "Then ye brought Surya forward who was lying hidden in the sea.",
      "original": "अत्रा समुद्र आ गूळ्हमा सूर्यमजभर्तन",
      "translit": "atrā samudra ā gūḷhamā sūryamajabhartana"
    },
    {
      "n": 16,
      "refId": "RV10-72:16",
      "text": "8. Eight are the Sons of Aditi who from her body sprang to life.",
      "original": "अष्टौ पुत्रासो अदितेर्ये जातास्तन्वस्परि ।",
      "translit": "aṣṭau putrāso aditerye jātāstanvaspari |"
    },
    {
      "n": 17,
      "refId": "RV10-72:17",
      "text": "With seven she went to meet the Gods she cast Martanda far away.",
      "original": "देवाँ उप प्रैत्सप्तभिः परा मार्ताण्डमास्यत्",
      "translit": "devām̐ upa praitsaptabhiḥ parā mārtāṇḍamāsyat"
    },
    {
      "n": 18,
      "refId": "RV10-72:18",
      "text": "9. So with her Seven Sons Aditi went forth to meet the earlier age.",
      "original": "सप्तभिः पुत्रैरदितिरुप प्रैत्पूर्व्यं युगम् ।",
      "translit": "saptabhiḥ putrairaditirupa praitpūrvyaṃ yugam |"
    },
    {
      "n": 19,
      "refId": "RV10-72:19",
      "text": "She brought Martanda thitherward to spring to life and die again.",
      "original": "प्रजायै मृत्यवे त्वत्पुनर्मार्ताण्डमाभरत्",
      "translit": "prajāyai mṛtyave tvatpunarmārtāṇḍamābharat"
    }
  ]
}
